  "overview": "**E-Trade Design Language** is a light-first design system anchored on `#ffffff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#1773b0` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `Inter` (30px display down to 14px body), unified by `0px` razor-sharp architectural corners and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **E-Trade**. Source: live stylesheet extraction (http://etrade.design/). Inventory: **91** colors, **8** typography steps, and **22** documented components (all rights reserved license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 22 component tokens with documented paddings: `10px`, `30px`, `2px 3px`, `1px`, `0`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#ffffff` cards; separate sibling sections using `#e2e2e2` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`0 1px 7px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.13)`) paired with `#e2e2e2` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#1773b0` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#ffffff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#1773b0` with `#f7f7f8` text (4.8:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Inter` headings with `Inter` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Enforce `0px` border-radius consistently across cards, inputs, and primary buttons.\n- Separate containers via `#ffffff` surface shifts and `#e2e2e2` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not apply rounded corners (> 0px) to structural containers or CTA buttons.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input-group-addon` fields and secondary buttons."
}
